  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1211 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nMostly clear skies and northerly winds are expected through this \nevening with some high clouds and light winds tonight. Winds shift \nto the southeast by tomorrow morning with some gusts over 20 mph \nacross far western Kansas by tomorrow afternoon. Cloud cover will \nincrease throughout the day tomorrow with mostly cloudy skies \nexpected by tomorrow evening. A weak disturbance will move through \nthe Rockies and into the Central High Plains tomorrow night bringing \na slight chance of precipitation across far western Kansas. \nTemperatures will be below freezing during this time and light snow \nis expected to fall.  However, the precipitation and duration will \nbe so short that little to no accumulation is expected. As for \ntemperatures, highs today and tomorrow are expected to reach into \nthe 40s with lows in the 20s tonight and tomorrow night. Even though \nthe winds will be light tonight, wind chills in the upper teens are \nexpected around sunrise with the exception of south central Kansas. \n\nThe remainder of the forecast looks dry with upper level ridging \nthrough mid week with an upper level trough digging into the \nNorthern Plains late week into this weekend. This will help push a \ncold front through the area late week shifting winds to the north. \nAs for temperatures, highs will generally be in the 40s through \nThursday with 50s to around 60 degrees Friday into this weekend. \nLows will be in the 20s with 30s returning this weekend.",
